HOW THE SYSTEM WORKS (STEP BY STEP)
------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 1 — USER LOGIN
-------------------
User creates account and logs in.

Why?
Because each user has:
• Their resumes
• Their job descriptions
• Their resume profile
• Their versions

------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 2 — RESUME UPLOAD
-----------------------
User uploads resume (PDF or DOCX).

System does:
1) Validate file
2) Extract text
3) Clean text
4) Detect sections:
   - Summary
   - Skills
   - Experience
   - Projects
   - Education
5) Extract:
   - Email
   - Phone
   - Links

Problem solved:
Some resumes have headings like:
"C O N T A C T"
System fixes that automatically.

------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 3 — ATS SCORE
-------------------
System gives score (0–100).

Score depends on:

• Section completeness
• Formatting safety
• Keywords
• Bullet structure
• Readability

User sees:

• Big score circle
• Breakdown
• Suggestions to improve

This helps user understand what is wrong.

------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 4 — BUILDER (STRUCTURED RESUME)
-------------------------------------
The uploaded resume is converted into:

Structured JSON format:

{
  personal,
  summary,
  skills,
  education,
  experience,
  projects
}

User can edit everything manually in a form.

Why Builder is powerful?

Because:
• Clean structure
• Easy to modify
• No formatting mess
• ATS friendly layout

------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 5 — INTERACTIVE RESUME VIEW
---------------------------------
User can preview resume.

Features:

• Skill chips (badges)
• Projects accordion (expand/collapse)
• Clean single column
• Print friendly

------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 6 — EXPORT PDF / DOCX
---------------------------
User can download:

PDF:
• Clean layout
• Clickable email
• Clickable phone
• Clickable links
• Section bookmarks
• ATS safe

DOCX:
• Word headings
• Collapsible project sections
• Hyperlinks
• Professional formatting

------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 7 — OPTIMIZER (AI WRITING ASSISTANT)
------------------------------------------

This is the smartest part.

User selects a bullet like:

"Created login system"

System rewrites into STAR format:

Example:
"Developed secure login system using JWT authentication, reducing unauthorized access by 30%."

STAR means:
S – Situation  
T – Task  
A – Action  
R – Result  

It makes bullets strong and measurable.

User can:
• Regenerate
• Compare before/after
• Apply changes directly

------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 8 — SUMMARY GENERATOR
---------------------------
User pastes Job Description.

System generates professional summary
based on:
• User skills
• Projects
• JD keywords

------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 9 — ATS FIX SUGGESTIONS
------------------------------
System compares:

Resume vs Job Description

Shows:
• Missing keywords
• Structure tips
• Improvement advice

------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 10 — SKILL GAP ROADMAP
----------------------------
System checks what JD requires
but resume does not show.

Then creates:

Week-by-week learning roadmap.

Example:

Week 1: Learn Docker
Week 2: Build Docker project
Week 3: Add bullet to resume

This makes CareerSetu AI a career coach.

------------------------------------------------------------

STEP 11 — COVER LETTER GENERATOR
---------------------------------
User enters:
• Company
• Role
• Job Description

System generates full cover letter.

User can:
• Edit content
• Copy
• Download PDF
• Download DOCX

